      en: "The Maryland Coast in southeastern Liberia stretches about 150 km along the Atlantic Ocean. It features sandy beaches, mangrove forests, and lagoons. The area is a critical nesting site for sea turtles, including the loggerhead and leatherback turtles. The Cavalla and Cestos rivers shape the coastline. Climate is tropical, with a rainy season from May to November. Fishing and tourism drive the local economy, but overfishing and coastal erosion pose threats. Nearby Cape Mount National Park offers some protection.",
